Universit\u00e9 Grenoble Alpes\nClose the mobile menu\nFR- Fran\u00e7ais\nEN- English\nDoctoral College\nPreparing a PhD\nThesis\nInternational\nCampus Life\nYou are here:\nHome\nPreparing a PhD\nEnrolment\nApplication and admission to a Doctoral School\nLire cette page en fran\u00e7ais\nPrerequisites\nTo apply, you must first have a thesis subject and there are two ways to proceed:\nChoose a subject from the current proposals, and submit your application according to the procedures indicated. Consult the websites of doctoral schools and research laboratories in your field, to find out about the subjects and funding available:\nPropose a thesis topic to a laboratory or Doctoral School (mainly in the arts, languages, humanities and social sciences). The subject will then be worked out with the future thesis supervisor;\nBe pre-selected by a thesis director and a host laboratory to carry out the research work;\nMeet the general conditions for registration in thesis defined by the decree of May 25, 2016 setting the national framework of training and the procedures leading to the issuance of the national PhD diploma namely:\nhold a French diploma conferring the degree of master at the end of a training programme establishing the aptitude for research;\nor hold a foreign diploma of equivalent level (obtained at the end of a training programme establishing the aptitude for research). In this case, your application will be examined by the Commission Dispenses et D\u00e9rogations Doctorales (CD3);\nor benefit from the validation of prior learning as provided for by the French Education Code.\nApplication\nApplication procedures vary from one doctoral school to another.\nPlease read their individual pages for guidance.\nED CSV: Chemistry and Life sciences\nED EEATS: Electronics, Electrical energy, Automatic control, Signal processing\nED IMEP\u00b2: Engineering - Material, Mechanics, Environment, Energetics, Processes, Production\nED ISCE: Engineering for Health, Cognition and the Environment\nED LLSH: Languages, Literature and Humanities\nED MSTII: Informatics and Mathematics\nED PHILO: Philosophy\nED PHYS: Physics\nED SE: Economics\nED SG: Management Sciences\nED SJ: Law\nED SHPT: Humanities, Political and Territorial Sciences\nED STEP: Earth, Environmental and Planetary Sciences\nAdmission\nIf your application has been selected by a Doctoral School, your Doctoral School will contact you about the admission phase.\nUpdated on October 2, 2026\nPrint\nShare\nShare this on Facebook\nShare this on LinkedIn\nPreparing a PhD\nThe doctorate\nDoctorate Enrolment\nSubjects & Funding\nChoose UGA\nResearch at UGA\nGrenoble Alpes, an Innovation Ecosystem\nDoctoral College - Universit\u00e9 Grenoble Alpes\nMaison du doctorat Jean Kuntzmann\n110 rue de la Chimie 38400 Saint-Martin-d'H\u00e8res\nFrance\nLegal notices\nContacts\nPersonal details\nCookies\nWebsite accessibility: not compliant\nFollow us\nFacebook\nYoutube\nX\nURL of the page\nhttps://doctorat.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/preparing-a-phd/doctorate-enrolment/application-and-admission-to-a-doctoral-school-890537.kjsp?RH=1611137559271\nPage title\nShare the link\nCopy\nCopied\nClose the modal window\nShare the URL of this page\nI recommend:\nConsultable at this address:\nLa page sera alors accessible depuis votre menu \"Mes favoris\".\nStop video\nPlay video\nMute\nPlay audio\nChat: A question?\nChatbot Robo Fabrica\nMatomo traffic statistics\nX (formerly Twitter)\nWhat are you looking for ?\nEnter a keyword and press Validate\nSearch on text :\nMore", "links": [["Universit\u00e9 Grenoble Alpes", "https://doctorat.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/universite-grenoble-alpes-/"], ["CSV Doctoral School", "https://doctorat.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/doctoral-schools/csv-doctoral-school/"], ["EEATS Doctoral School", "https://doctorat.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/doctoral-schools/eeats-doctoral-school/"], ["I-MEP\u00b2 Doctoral School", "https://doctorat.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/doctoral-schools/i-mep-doctoral-school/"], 